WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
"Where to Find Taurine and the Best Source"

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.080
Foods that contain
the highest levels of taurine

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.920
come from the sea,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.920
particularly seaweed
and shellfish.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.200
Here it is graphically,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.160
so you can see how shellfish
compared to other meat.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.360
The most concentrated source,
though, is dried nori,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.560
the seaweed sheets
used to make sushi.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.520
Land plants, however,
have negligible amounts.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.400
So, a singular focus
on increasing dietary taurine

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.200
risks driving
poor nutritional choices,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.800
because plant-rich diets

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.120
are associated with
human health and longevity.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.520
I mean, energy drinks
have taurine too,

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.600
but slamming monster,
Red Bull, Rockstar, Cocaine

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.640
is probably not the best option.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.880
The best choice
would probably be

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.880
to eat a healthy
plant-based diet

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.120
with supplemental taurine.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.880
It’s such a simple molecule,

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.000
it can be
inexpensively synthesized.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.320
So, you can just get
pure taurine powder.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.720
Here’s how it all breaks down.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.560
We can start with concentration.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.800
Pure taurine
obviously has the most,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.240
then dried nori,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.240
then an average of clams,
oysters, mussels, and scallops,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.960
then the average
across nine energy drinks,

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.560
then fin fish,

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.120
including the highest,
yellow sea bream,

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.040
down to tuna,
one of the lowest.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.480
Then an average
of chicken, beef, and pork.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.240
Nori’s looking pretty good

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.240
until you realize
how light it is.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.600
To get one gram of taurine,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.280
you’d have to eat
10 servings a day,

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.920
which is 40 sheets of nori,

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.080
which, even if
you could stomach it,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.000
would exceed your recommended
iodine intake for the day.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.600
The easiest way to get a gram

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.640
would be a quarter teaspoon
of pure taurine powder,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.600
though one can of most
energy drinks would do it,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.560
but then there’s the issue

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.200
of added sugars
or artificial sweeteners.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.120
Two daily servings
of shellfish

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.600
is a lot of shellfish,
but certainly doable.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.200
Easier than eating eight
daily servings of regular fish

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.880
or 18 servings a day
of land animals.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.800
Here’s the cost comparison.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.880
This is where
taurine powder really shines,

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.920
at as little as a penny per day
when bought in bulk,

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.440
it’s 50 times cheaper
than the next on the list.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.040
Now, I used a combination
of canned and fresh shellfish

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.320
for this comparison.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.720
If you just did,
like, canned clams,

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.320
it would be
more like $2.50 a day.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.160
In terms of saturated fat
and cholesterol,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.280
shellfish are extremely lean,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.200
though the dietary guidelines

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.680
recommend that dietary
cholesterol consumption

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.320
be as low as possible,

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.680
90 is less
than half an egg yolk.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.000
Allergies are an issue for some.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.720
Shellfish is actually
the most common type

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.480
of food allergy
in the United States,

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.000
affecting about 1 in 35 people,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.080
though it may
be as high as 1 in 10

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.400
depending on
the method of diagnosis.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.520
Allergies to land-based meat
are rare,

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.400
unless you’ve been bitten
by certain types of ticks.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.040
Foodborne illness
can also be a problem,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.360
particularly since
shellfish, like oysters,

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.440
are sometimes eaten raw.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.360
Usually,
it’s just gastroenteritis,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.720
but it can sometimes develop
into serious infections.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.640
Shellfish are filter-feeders,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.720
so, they just pick up
and concentrate pathogens

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.000
from the environment.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.200
Most outbreaks are actually
from human fecal pathogens

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.600
from sewage
that gets into the water,

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.920
or the overboard disposal
of feces from boats.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.680
I guess I never really
thought about that,

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.720
but, like, most crews
from oyster-harvesting boats

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.960
were just, like, tossing
their waste overboard,

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.640
and it may come back
to bite them.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.000
How common
is contamination of shellfish

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.560
with foodborne
human fecal viruses,

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:43.520
like norovirus,

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:46.160
the most common cause
of foodborne gastroenteritis?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.120
Nearly one in three
samples of shellfish

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.800
carries this kind
of fecal contamination

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.160
that can make us sick,

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.400
yet, most consumers
ignore the fact

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.640
that shellfish
usually comes from places

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.440
polluted by
untreated human waste.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.640
Though fecal contamination
is also found in 85 percent

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.320
of retail ground beef
and turkey,

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.200
about half of chicken,
and a third of pork.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.520
Thankfully,
those meats are cooked,

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.760
but, still,
contaminated poultry products

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.320
probably cause the most
food poisoning deaths,

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.480
not shellfish.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.760
Then, anytime you’re talking
about the aquatic food chain,

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.400
there are industrial pollutants.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.280
Pollution of the oceans
is widespread and worsening,

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.120
and pollutants include
toxic heavy metals,

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.960
like mercury,
microplastics,

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.760
and industrial toxins,
like PCBs.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.720
Yes, we’ve been eating shellfish

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.440
for more than
a hundred thousand years,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.080
but that was before
we so polluted our waterways.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.280
Shellfish pump and filter
such large quantities of water

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.800
in their feeding processes

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.240
that they just tend
to accumulate

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.960
a lot of contaminants,
like heavy metals.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.680
So, the consumption
of contaminated shellfish

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.400
can lead to neurological
and developmental defects,

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.720
reproductive and
gastrointestinal disorders,

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.680
and in extreme cases, death.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.000
That does seem a little extreme.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.400
They’re talking
about contamination

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.120
with algal toxins.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.160
While filter-feeding,

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.640
shellfish
can ingest toxic algae,

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.120
which can produce a hundred
different natural toxins.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.440
So, the shellfish
can accumulate these toxins

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.760
and pass them on to consumers.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.960
So, although we refer to them
as shellfish toxins,

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.520
they’re actually no more
from the shellfish themselves

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.640
than the human
fecal viruses were.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.640
When humans
ingest different toxins

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.080
accumulated in seafood,

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.040
they may exhibit
different poisoning syndromes.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.680
There’s paralytic
shellfish poisoning,

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.080
amnesic shellfish poisoning,

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.920
neurotoxic shellfish poisoning,

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.960
and diarrhetic
shellfish poisoning.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.120
Symptoms-wise,
these can include

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.440
abdominal pain, vomiting,
diarrhea, severe headaches,

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.240
confusion, agitation,
sleepiness, memory loss,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.800
coma, loss of coordination,
excessive scratching, tremors,

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.240
heart arrhythmias, seizures,
lethargy, inappetence,

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.960
I’d never heard that word
for loss of appetite,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.040
blindness, muscular twitches,

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.560
behavioral changes,
convulsions,

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.840
and death,
sometimes within hours.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.360
No antidotes are available.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:13.520
Sometimes,
neuropsychological symptoms

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.840
can last for years.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.080
Some of the toxins
may be carcinogenic,

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.560
linked to a variety
of different cancers.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.240
This may help explain
cohort studies

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.560
that found associations
between colorectal cancer

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.640
and the consumption
of shellfish and shrimp.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.080
But, of course,
it could also be

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.760
the industrial pollutants.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.320
The bad news is
that toxic algae blooms

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.480
are getting worse,
thanks to climate change.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.600
But the good news is that

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.200
the U.S. Food
and Drug Administration

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.280
has established
a surveillance program

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.280
to test for toxins.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.000
So, there are regulatory limits.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.960
Unfortunately, despite
strong regulatory limits

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.760
protecting people
from acute poisoning,

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.200
there is a growing
body of evidence

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.840
suggesting there are
significant health consequences

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.440
following repeated exposures

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:59.200
to levels
of an amnesic neurotoxin

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.720
known as domoic acid,

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.480
even when below
current safety guidelines.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.320
Those in the Pacific Northwest

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.960
who eat a lot
of razor clams, for example,

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.480
with presumed safe levels,
were found to be at risk

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:15.200
for clinically significant
memory problems.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.240
They are five to six times
more likely to have problems

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.600
with everyday memory,

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.080
like, having to check whether
you actually did something,

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.480
or forgetting to tell
someone something important,

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.880
or being forgetful day to day.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.440
The toxin doesn’t seem
to be affected by cooking,

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.480
and the "very high"
levels of consumption

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.280
were just more than
15 clams a month.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.360
So, Washington State
tells its residents

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:38.640
to eat less than that,

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.880
but to reach
a gram a day of taurine

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.880
you’d have to eat 10 a day,
300 a month.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.840
The bottom line is that
even at levels deemed "safe"

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.840
under current regulatory limits,

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.480
algal toxins
may not make mollusks

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:56.015
the best source
for taurine supplementation.

